{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-04T10:09:22.146Z","data":{"text":"Both the task verify and the proposal verify pass. Summary of changes:\n\n**`src/cli/serve-actions.ts`** (new) — `createWebActionRunner({ cwd, config }, commands?)` maps `approve`/`land`/`reject`/`retry` to the CLI command functions, gives each request its own collecting `stdout`/`stderr`, and turns a `CommandError` (exit code, message, `next`) or any other throw (`Error: <message>`, next null) into a `WebActionResult`. It never rejects or writes to a process stream.\n\n**`src/cli/serve.ts`** — passes `runAction: createWebActionRunner({ cwd, config })` to `startWebServer`; `--export` is untouched.\n\n**`src/cli/index.ts`** — `serve` description now says the dashboard can approve, land, reject and retry.\n\n**`README.md`** — the `## Commands` serve line and the Delivery Dashboard prose are no longer read-only.\n\n**`tests/serve-actions.test.ts`** (new) — recording-table tests for each verb and for `CommandError`/generic failures with per-request writers and a process-stream tripwire; default-table `reject`/`retry` of missing change `999`; and an end-to-end `serveCommand` approval through `POST /api/actions/001` that matches a twin `approveCommand` on `.run/approved` and event types.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/146-web-write-actions/.run/results/2.md`."}}
